            <ArticleTitle>Preparation of Polyfunctional Naphthyridines by Cobalt-Catalyzed Cross-Couplings of Halogenated Naphthyridines with Magnesium and Zinc Organometallics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6384-6387</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03242</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>CoCl2 (5%) catalyzes cross-couplings of various halogenated naphthyridines with alkyl- and arylmagnesium halides. Also, arylzinc halides undergo smooth cross-couplings with various naphthyridines in the presence of CoCl2·2LiCl (5%) and sodium formate (50%), leading to polyfunctional arylated naphthyridines. Two of these arylated naphthyridines are highly fluorescent, with quantum efficiencies reaching 95% and long excited-state lifetimes of up to 12 ns.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
